# 6. What is CompletableFuture? Have you used asynchronous programming?

> **"CompletableFuture is a Java 8 feature used for asynchronous and non-blocking programming. It allows tasks to execute in the background without blocking the main thread and supports chaining operations using methods like thenApply(), thenAccept(), thenCompose(), and combining multiple tasks using allOf(). It also provides exception handling using exceptionally() and handle(). In my project, I used CompletableFuture to call multiple external REST APIs in parallel. Instead of making sequential calls, all APIs were executed asynchronously, and their responses were combined. This reduced the overall API response time and improved application performance."**

