### 14. What is Auto Configuration?

> **"Auto Configuration is one of the main features of Spring Boot. It automatically configures beans based on the dependencies available in the application's classpath. For example, if Spring Boot detects `spring-boot-starter-web`, it automatically configures DispatcherServlet, Jackson, and an embedded Tomcat server. This eliminates most XML and Java configuration, allowing developers to focus on business logic."**

