### 15. What is Spring Bean Scope?

> **"A Spring Bean is an object managed by the Spring IoC container. The default scope is Singleton, meaning only one instance of the bean exists throughout the application. Other scopes include Prototype, Request, Session, and Application. In my project, we mostly used the default Singleton scope for service and repository beans because they are stateless and thread-safe."**

---

### 16. What is the Spring Bean Lifecycle?

> **"The Spring Bean lifecycle starts when the container creates the bean, injects its dependencies, and invokes initialization methods such as `@PostConstruct` or `InitializingBean`. The bean remains available for application use until the application shuts down, after which Spring calls destruction methods like `@PreDestroy` before removing the bean. Understanding this lifecycle helps when initializing resources or performing cleanup operations."**

