## 29. What is Chunk Processing in Spring Batch?

> **"Chunk processing is the default processing model in Spring Batch. Instead of processing one record at a time or loading the entire dataset into memory, Spring Batch reads a fixed number of records, processes them, and writes them as a single transaction. For example, with a chunk size of 100, it reads 100 records, processes them, writes them, commits the transaction, and then continues with the next 100. In our project, chunk processing improved performance and reduced memory consumption while processing large CSV files."**

---

## 30. Why did you use Spring Batch?

> **"We used Spring Batch because it provides robust support for processing large volumes of data. It offers chunk processing, retry and skip mechanisms, restartability, transaction management, scheduling support, and detailed job monitoring. These features made it ideal for our ETL and file-processing requirements."**

